  <text>
    <body>
      <p>The Garbutt family made chains in <ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref> and <ref target="civic?id=Berkley%20Street">Berkley Street</ref> for almost sixty years. J. Garbutt, chain maker, is listed at 17 Leicester Street from 1863, and John Garbutt, chain and hames maker, there to 1880, then at 59 Leicester Street (55 in 1905) from 1890 to 1905.</p>
      <p>In Berkley Street the directories list Joseph Garbutt, chain and hame maker, at No. 40, later No. 44, from 1869 to 1873, and John Garbutt, chain maker, at No. 2 from 1871 to 1885, then No. 30 from 1890 and No. 38 in 1920. With two John Garbutts listed in the same years, the directories seem to show more than one member of the family in the trade.</p>
